-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS ONE, AND HOW TO CHANGE IT

This is deliberately the most restrictive sensible default, chosen because
selling this was named as a possible goal and because the choice is
asymmetric:

    all rights reserved -> MIT      you can do this whenever you like
    MIT -> all rights reserved      you cannot; every copy already out
                                    stays MIT forever

So this preserves every option, including the ones you have not decided on.
It is not a recommendation to keep it closed. If you would rather people
could use and build on it, replace this file with the MIT licence text and
say so in the README — that is a two-minute change and it is yours to make.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS. This licence covers the code in this repository.
It does not cover the dependencies in requirements.txt, which carry their
own licences (mostly MIT, Apache-2.0 and BSD) and remain the property of
their authors. The models under models/ come from openWakeWord and Silero
and carry their own terms. Anyone intending to SELL this should read those
before shipping, in particular the terms of the wake-word and VAD models
and of the Claude, Groq and edge-tts services this depends on at runtime —
each of those has its own rules about redistribution and about commercial
use on someone else's behalf.
